WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.550
Let's go next to our caller from the seven
Oh six area code.

00:00:03.550 --> 00:00:05.879
Who is calling today from seven zero six.

00:00:05.879 --> 00:00:07.529
Oh, Hey David.

00:00:07.529 --> 00:00:10.309
This is Kyle from Orlando, Florida.

00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:11.309
Hey Kyle.

00:00:11.309 --> 00:00:12.309
What's up?

00:00:12.309 --> 00:00:13.309
Hey.

00:00:13.309 --> 00:00:18.460
Um, so, uh, I work for Disney and, um, as
part of our union contract, we were able to

00:00:18.460 --> 00:00:22.710
get a $15 an hour, uh, by 2021.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:23.710
Right.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:31.500
Um, which I think is great, but, um, you know,
in 2016 we were having the debate about $15

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:32.540
being the minimum wage.

00:00:32.540 --> 00:00:37.800
Uh, but you know, given that inflation is
a thing, uh, shouldn't we be talking about

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.320
$20 an hour now?

00:00:39.320 --> 00:00:40.780
And tying that to inflation.

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:41.780
Yeah.

00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:46.790
So this is something that I've mentioned many
times when the $15 an hour minimum wage thing

00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:53.800
started, and it was often not for right now,
but let's get up to $15 by some future date.

00:00:53.800 --> 00:00:54.800
A lot of the [inaudible]

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:57.570
outreach, a lot of the outrage was just bad
faith outrage.

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:02.370
Some of the outrage seemed not to take into
account that merely because of inflation,

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:07.549
it would have really only been like $12 at
the time that the conversation started, or

00:01:07.549 --> 00:01:10.909
$13 at the time that, you know, the conversation's
been going on at a lot of different be tied

00:01:10.909 --> 00:01:16.439
to, to inflation automatically because otherwise
this conversation will literally never end.

00:01:16.439 --> 00:01:17.740
Right, right.

00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:24.380
The, I mean, do you think like shooting for
$20 an hour anyways, and then, I mean, maybe

00:01:24.380 --> 00:01:29.749
we can say, Oh, well the compromise will be,
you know, $15 an hour.

00:01:29.749 --> 00:01:33.360
Um, just as a way to, I guess to get ahead
of the Republicans.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:34.360
I don't know that I would just

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:38.979
throw out a random number, but there are good
studies that say, listen, if we had indexed

00:01:38.979 --> 00:01:45.439
to inflation going back to 1968, it should
now be, you know, like 1770 an hour.

00:01:45.439 --> 00:01:46.439
That's where it should be.

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:47.469
Let's negotiate from there.

00:01:47.469 --> 00:01:50.939
And, and here's something that now a lot of
people on the right won't, won't like that,

00:01:50.939 --> 00:01:53.880
but let me say something that a lot of people
on the left won't like, which I think does

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:54.920
make sense.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:55.920
I've said before

00:01:55.920 --> 00:02:01.890
four, I think that the minimum wage needs
to be regionalized to some degree because

00:02:01.890 --> 00:02:08.459
if you have a low cost of living state where
you're talking about going from seven 50 to

00:02:08.459 --> 00:02:13.510
15, that is very different than a high cost
of living state where you're talking about

00:02:13.510 --> 00:02:15.930
going from 12 to 15.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:20.040
So I do think that there is something too
we should look at.

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:24.430
I don't know if it's on a state by state level,
Metro areas or whatever the case may be, but

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:30.800
there should be consideration given to both
cost of living, uh, as well as, um, uh, what

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:33.360
the, the current minimum wage is.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.670
I'm not advocating for the wage to be seven
25 anywhere to be clear, but I am saying that

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:44.349
in some places, 15 may not actually be the
right number to achieve what it is that, that

00:02:44.349 --> 00:02:46.200
we should be looking to achieve.

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:47.200
Okay.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.879
Well thanks David.

00:02:49.879 --> 00:02:51.040
All right, appreciate the call.

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:51.560
Thank you so much

